;; One work-unit for bin/fleet-sandbox-dispatch.cljk.
;;
;; :pin is the commit the sandbox is built from — the dispatcher fetches THIS
;; sha fresh from the GitHub API, never a local checkout (which drifts). Keep it
;; in sync with manifest/west.yml's entry for the repo.
{:work-id "kd-ops-by-actor"
 :unit    "kotoba-lang/kotoba-delta"
 :repo    "kotoba-lang/kotoba-delta"
 :pin     "c8c405abda731e5889aff3ae2a18ac208b375bb5"
 :node    "naphtali"
 :requires #{:nbb :git}
 :allow-push true
 :test-cmd "kbb --backend sci --classpath src:test run-tests.cljs"
 :ttl-ms  1800000
 :protected-paths [".github/" ".git/" "package.json" "package-lock.json"]
 :budget  {:max-turns 12 :max-tool-calls 30 :max-tokens 4000
           :deadline-ms 1200000 :test-timeout-ms 180000}
 :prompt
 "Task: add one small pure helper to this repository, with a test.

  1. In src/delta/op.cljc add a function `ops-by-actor`:
     (defn ops-by-actor [ops actor] ...) — returns, in log order, the ops in
     `ops` whose :op/actor equals `actor`. Give it a short docstring. It must be
     pure and must not change any existing function.
  2. In test/delta/op_test.cljc add a deftest named `ops-by-actor-filters`
     asserting that (a) a known actor yields only that actor's ops, in order,
     and (b) an unknown actor yields an empty result.
  3. Run the tests and make sure they pass.

  Touch only those two files."}
